# Rules 8 and 12: a checkout must be byte-identical on Windows and on
# ubuntu-latest. Anything hashed into a lock file breaks otherwise.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf rewrites LF to CRLF when checking out on Windows.
# The vendored OFL texts then differ from the blobs git stored, their sha256
# stops matching theme/fonts/fonts.lock.json, and the font test fails. It fails
# only on Windows, which is the worst shape for a bug: green in CI, red on the
# maintainer's machine. A fresh clone caught this one.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored build inputs are hashed. Git must not rewrite a single byte of them,
# including the license texts.
theme/fonts/** -text

*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary

# The Makefile is tab-sensitive. Never let a filter touch it.
Makefile -text
